<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>MM-embedding RAG Comparison</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare RAG performance using two multimodal embeddings: <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">voyage-multimodal-3</span> and <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gme-Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct</span>, with results reported in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ E.2 MM-embedding RAG Comparison ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ UniDoc-Bench: A Unified Benchmark for Document-Centric Multimodal RAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Table <a href="#A5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ E.2 MM-embedding RAG Comparison ‣ Appendix E Additional Experiments ‣ UniDoc-Bench: A Unified Benchmark for Document-Centric Multimodal RAG" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. While <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">voyage-multimodal-3</span> achieves slightly lower recall but higher precision in retrieval compared to <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gme-Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct</span>, it delivers better overall performance when integrated into MM-RAG.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Retrieval performance (Precision@10 / Recall@10) and end-to-end performance (<span id="A5.T8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Recall</span> using retrieved-top-10 and retrieved-top-20 candidates) of two MM-RAG systems on 200 QA pairs across eight domains, with average recall reported across all domains.</figcaption>
